From: Matt
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a4xx: look up OCMEM on the GPU node

The "sram" phandle is on the GPU node, but a4xx passes the DRM device
(the display controller, or nothing when headless), so of_get_ocmem()
never finds it ("Cannot look up sram phandle") and the A420/A430 runs
without GMEM. a3xx already passes the GPU platform device.
---
diff -ruN a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a4xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a4xx_gpu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a4xx_gpu.c	2026-10-27 20:24:48.016016421 +0100
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a4xx_gpu.c	2026-10-27 20:24:48.018032591 +0100
@@ -688,7 +688,7 @@
 							     a4xx_registers;
 
 	/* if needed, allocate gmem: */
-	ret = adreno_gpu_ocmem_init(dev->dev, adreno_gpu,
+	ret = adreno_gpu_ocmem_init(&adreno_gpu->base.pdev->dev, adreno_gpu,
 				    &a4xx_gpu->ocmem);
 	if (ret)
 		goto fail;
